{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "# What Are Variables"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Learning Objectives",
        "",
        "- Understand variables",
        "- Learn var, let and const",
        "- Store values"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Introduction",
        "",
        "Variables are named containers used to store data."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "console.log(\"Welcome to JavaScript Variables\");"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## What is a Variable?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "let name = \"Sachin\";",
        "console.log(name);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Why Do We Need Variables?"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "let age = 25;",
        "console.log(age);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Declaring Variables"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "let city = \"Delhi\";",
        "console.log(city);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The var Keyword"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "var country = \"India\";",
        "console.log(country);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The let Keyword"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "let language = \"JavaScript\";",
        "console.log(language);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## The const Keyword"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "const PI = 3.14159;",
        "console.log(PI);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Variable Naming Rules"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "let firstName = \"John\";",
        "let _age = 20;",
        "let $salary = 5000;",
        "",
        "console.log(firstName);",
        "console.log(_age);",
        "console.log($salary);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Invalid Variable Names"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "// let 1name = \"John\";",
        "// let first-name = \"John\";",
        "// let let = 10;"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Reassigning Variables"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "let score = 10;",
        "score = 20;",
        "",
        "console.log(score);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Constants Cannot Be Reassigned"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "const COUNTRY = \"India\";",
        "console.log(COUNTRY);",
        "",
        "// COUNTRY = \"USA\";"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Best Practices"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "let studentName = \"Alice\";",
        "let totalMarks = 450;",
        "let isPassed = true;",
        "",
        "console.log(studentName);",
        "console.log(totalMarks);",
        "console.log(isPassed);"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Exercise"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "execution_count": null,
      "metadata": {},
      "outputs": [],
      "source": [
        "// Create these variables:",
        "//",
        "// yourName",
        "// yourAge",
        "// yourCity",
        "// yourCountry",
        "//",
        "// Print all values."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Summary",
        "",
        "- Variables store values.",
        "- Prefer let and const.",
        "- Avoid var in modern JavaScript."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {},
      "source": [
        "## Practice Questions",
        "",
        "1. What is a variable?",
        "2. Difference between var, let and const?",
        "3. Why use const?",
        "4. What are naming rules?"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "metadata": {
    "kernelspec": {
      "display_name": "Node.js",
